Apache Spark
Apache spark is big data processing system
Where huge data cannot processed on single system for that system is distributed into multiple sub system called as distributed system

What is Databricks 
Databricks is managed solution for apache spark. 

Databricks Unity Catalog
It is present inside Unity Metastore. it is just like database in SQL. Unity Catlog contain schema inside it tables, volume, model, views 

Databricks Volumes
Volume which are inside unity catalog that governs data directly from non tabular data (Managed volumes) such as files like JSON, CSV, Parquet etc
It also govern data from cloud storage object (External Volume) like AWS, Azure etc. 

Databricks Architecture
It contains Control Pane and Compute Pane
Control Pane: Main UI of databricks which contains user profile, workspace, catalog etc 
Compute Pane: Data processing all operation regarding data which are inside it
2 types of Architecture:
Classic Architecture:
It has control and compute pane but all work is manually done by compute pane like resource selection to processed data
This architecture used when data is huge, and our budget is less. 
Serverless Architecture:
It has control and compute pane but this architecture automatically perform scaling up and down resources as requires for data processing. 
It is used when data is less but this architecture is costly as compared to previous one. 

